    <section class="quiz" id="routine">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The two-minute routine finder</p>
        <h2>What does your skin need today?</h2>
        <p>Choose the options that sound most like you. This educational guide offers a simple starting point, not a medical diagnosis.</p>
      </div>
      <form action="#recommendations" method="get">
        <fieldset>
          <legend>1. How does your skin usually feel after cleansing?</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="skin" value="dry" required> Tight, flaky, or dry</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="skin" value="oily"> Shiny or oily</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="skin" value="combination"> Oily in some areas and dry in others</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="skin" value="sensitive"> Easily irritated or uncomfortable</label>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>2. How much time do you spend outside?</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="sun" value="low" required> Mostly indoors with short trips outside</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="sun" value="medium"> A few hours outdoors most days</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="sun" value="high"> Long periods outdoors or exercising in the sun</label>
        </fieldset>
        <button class="button" type="submit">View my routine</button>
      </form>
      <div id="recommendations" class="feature-panel" style="margin-top:25px">
        <h3>Your routine starting point</h3>
        <p>For dry or sensitive skin, start with a gentle cleanser, apply a moisturizer while skin is slightly damp, and finish with broad-spectrum SPF 30 or higher. For oily or combination skin, use a lighter layer of moisturizer rather than skipping it. If you spend time outside, reapply sunscreen at least every two hours and after swimming or sweating, following the label directions.</p>
        <p>Your answers are not processed by a recommendation engine; use the guidance above to choose the steps that fit your needs.</p>
      </div>
